# Funds Manager AI workflow

Follow this loop for every delivery. Do not skip steps unless the user explicitly says so.

## 1. Ticket (GitHub) — **first step when starting work**

- Work from a **GitHub issue** on [Project #5](https://github.com/users/kgz/projects/5/views/1).
- **Immediately** move cards to **In progress**:

```bash
./bin/board-status.sh in-progress <issue-num>
```

- When closing: `./bin/board-status.sh done <issue-numbers...>`
- **Keep board in sync with code:** update `bin/od-redesign-tracker.tsv` when delivery status changes, then run `./bin/board-audit.sh --apply` (or `./bin/board-audit.sh` to check drift only).
- Board lifecycle: **Ready** → **In progress** (start work) → **In review** (code complete on branch / PR open) → **Done** (merged + issue closed).
- PR must reference them with `Closes #N`.

## 2. New branch (from `main`)

```bash
git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b feature/<issue>-<short-slug>
```

## 3. Spec (OpenSpec — on `main` first)

- On **`main`**: `/opsx:propose` → `openspec/changes/<change-name>/`
- Then checkout the delivery branch and commit spec artifacts there.

## 4. Explore / apply (on delivery branch)

- Optional: `/opsx:explore`
- **`/opsx:apply`** on `feature/<n>-<slug>` only — implement `tasks.md`, check off `- [x]` as you go.

## Open Design runs (must show in OD UI)

Never start OD runs with raw `curl` and a `project` field — they will **not** appear in the project chat.

Use:

```bash
./bin/od-design-run.sh --issue <n> "Design prompt…"
# or per-issue thread:
./bin/od-design-run.sh --issue 225 --new-conversation "#225 Report snapshots" "Design …"
```

Requires OD dev server (`pnpm exec tools-dev run web --web-port 29013 --daemon-port 28585`). Watch URL is printed after start.

## 5. Test, docs & quality

User-facing changes are **not done** until docs (and e2e where applicable) ship in the **same PR** as the code.

### Code

- `cargo test` in `app/`, `database/`, and affected `crates/`
- `cd frontend && pnpm run build` before PR when UI changes
- Manual QA for affected routes before PR

### Docs + e2e (required for UI / behaviour users can see)

Follow `.cursor/skills/document-feature/SKILL.md`:

- [ ] Update or add **User guide** page(s) under `docs-site/user-guide/` (setup changes → `docs-site/guide/`)
- [ ] Lead with **what doing this does** (effects), and **cross-link** related User guide pages both ways
- [ ] Screenshots from Playwright mocks/demo data + `screenshots.manifest.json` (alt + expects)
- [ ] Playwright e2e for the happy path (`frontend/e2e/…`) when the ticket changes interactive flow
- [ ] `TO COME` callouts for anything not shipped yet
- [ ] No issue/epic/board links or AI-ish Unicode in published pages
- [ ] `cd docs-site && pnpm build` passes
- [ ] Wire sidebar/nav if a new User guide page was added

### Dead-end review (required before In review)

For each new user-facing capability, list what it **drives** (predictions, liabilities, KPIs, another screen, export, etc.).

| Outcome | Action |
|---------|--------|
| Drives something real | Document the effect + link to that User guide page (and update the other page to link back) |
| Intentionally reminder / calendar-only | OK if that is the product intent - say so clearly; use `TO COME` only if more is planned |
| Looks finished but drives nothing | **Not done** - file a follow-up GitHub issue, link it from the parent ticket, board it (`Ready` or `Backlog`), mention the follow-up in the PR |

OpenSpec `tasks.md` for UI work **must** include docs + e2e + dead-end review checklist items (not a follow-up ticket by default, unless the dead-end review creates one).

GitHub Pages deploys from `main` via `.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml` when `docs-site/**` changes merge.

## Git commits & PRs

- Never add `Co-authored-by`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or any Cursor/agent attribution to commits or PR bodies.
- Use plain `git commit -m` / heredoc only — no `--trailer`.
- If attribution is appended by the environment, amend to remove it before pushing.

## 6. Pull request + link ticket

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base main --head feature/<n>-<slug> \
  --title "..." --body "## Summary\n...\n\nCloses #<issue>"
```

## 7. Archive spec (before or right after merge)

- `openspec archive <change-name> -y` (syncs specs and moves to archive)
- Or manually sync `openspec/specs/` and move to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`

## 8. Merge

- Merge PR after review (and CI if present).

## 9. Ticket → Done

- `./bin/board-status.sh done <issue-numbers...>`
- `gh issue close <n> --repo kgz/Funds-Manager`

